# Registers

The Register File contains 8 registers:

R0
R1
R2
R3
R4
R5
R6
R7

Each register stores 8 bits.

---

# Write Operation

A register is written when "Write Enable" is active.

Example:

Write Address = 001
Write Data = 00011001
Write Enable = 1

Clock ↑

After the clock edge:

R1 = 00011001

---

# Read Operation

The Register File has two read ports.

This allows two registers to be read at the same time.

Example:

Read Address A = 001
Read Address B = 010

If:

R1 = 25
R2 = 10

then:

Read Data A = 25
Read Data B = 10

This is useful for CPU instructions that operate on two operands.

