# CPU Connection

A Register File is an important component inside a CPU.

A simplified CPU datapath can be represented as:

             Instruction
                  │
                  ▼
          ┌───────────────┐
          │ Register File │
          └───────┬───────┘
                  │
             ┌────┴────┐
             │         │
             ▼         ▼
          Operand A  Operand B
             │         │
             └────┬────┘
                  ▼
                ALU
                  │
                  ▼
               Result


For example, an instruction equivalent to:

R3 = R1 + R2

could work conceptually like this:


R1 ─────► Read Port A ──┐
                        │
                        ▼
                       ALU ───► R3
                        ▲
                        │
R2 ─────► Read Port B ──┘

This is one of the reasons Register Files are important when learning CPU architecture.

